    "blind_description": "This is a line-drawn corner storefront, shown in angular perspective, on a blank background.\n\nVisible elements:\n- Above the building floats an L-shaped two-panel sign, with a complete outline; each angled panel contains the legible hand-drawn text **CAFÉ**. The sign is disconnected from the building below.\n- The building has two meeting facade planes forming a corner. Outer wall outlines are complete; the lower corner and base edges are drawn.\n- Centered at the corner is a double door: a complete outer rectangular frame, two narrow door leaves divided by a center line, and two small vertical pull handles. No door fill/detail is shown.\n- On each side facade is a large four-pane window, drawn as a rectangle with one vertical and one horizontal mullion crossing; pane divisions are complete. The far outer side edges of the walls extend beyond the windows.\n- Above the door/windows runs an awning/valance structure: a long rectangular segmented fascia, divided into panels by short vertical lines. Its lower edge is a continuous scalloped/wavy curtain line, with repeated U-shaped loops. Two small open triangular support shapes are drawn under the fascia near each outer end, but their attachment to wall/awning is only implied by line adjacency.\n- In the foreground, two identical small round cafe tables are fully outlined: circular tops, single central stem, and circular bases. They are not connected to the building or to each other.\n- No people, interior contents, color, shading, ground plane, or side/rear building structure are visible. The scene is a clean exterior front-corner elevation only.",
